// Forced-above dynamics (@x.up). Exercises every above-staff dynamic path, which
// no other fixture touches: an on-staff @f.up / @mf.up sits above the staff while
// @p / @f on neighbours stay below (measure 1); above dynamics over high,
// ledger-lined notes are note-governed and rise with the pitch (measure 2); and
// two voices' @p.up / @f.up on the SAME column stack outward, away from the staff
// (measure 3). The above baseline clears the staff/notes by the glyph DESCENDER,
// matching LilyPond's \dynamicUp (see DynamicEngraver.TextDescent). Absolute octave
// mode keeps the pitches explicit.
octave absolute
title "Above-staff dynamics"
part m { clef treble }
section S {
  m {
    b4@f.up c'@p e'@mf.up f'@f |
    g'4@ff.up a'@f.up b'@p.up c''@mf.up |
    voice { e'4@f.up f' g' a' } voice { b4@p.up c' d' e' } |
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "above-dynamics" { staff m }
